<title>BELGIUM: BELGIUM SHARES EU POLE POSITION ON LOW INFLATION.</title>
<headline>BELGIUM SHARES EU POLE POSITION ON LOW INFLATION.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium shared pole position with Finland in April in having the lowest inflation rate in the 15-nation European Union, the European Commission's statistics office, Eurostat, said on Friday.</p>
<p>The two countries had inflation rates of just 0.9 percent in the month, followed by France on 1.0 percent, Luxembourg 1.1 percent, Germany, the Netherland and Sweden on 1.2 percent, Austria 1.3 percent and Denmark on 1.5 percent -- the average for the bloc as a whole.</p>
<p>All others were above the average, with Greece bringing up the rear on 5.7 percent.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
